ening.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 66 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Sarah Huckabee Sanders (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Governor Sarah Huckabee Sanders enters the general election as a heavy favorite for a second term. Arkansas leans roughly fifteen points Republican, and Sanders carries the added weight of incumbency in a state she won comfortably in 2022. Every major rating outlet, including the Cook Political Report, Inside Elections, and Sabato's Crystal Ball, places the race in the Solid or Safe Republican column, and prediction markets give Democrats only a two to three percent chance. State Senator Fredrick Love, the Democratic nominee, shows no reported fundraising, and a Libertarian is also on the ballot.\n\nThe one caution sign is an August Hendrix College survey of likely voters that put Sanders ahead by only five points, far inside her 2022 margin, and local coverage has noted her approval softening. Even so, with no fresh polling since and no reported money behind the challenge, Republicans remain strong favorites here.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0236, "margin": -11.99}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0374, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0306, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0358, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0294, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.026, "margin": -13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0389, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0411, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0411, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0419, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0317, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0391, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0382, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0238, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0323, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2